From-scratch safe Rust QR Code Model 2 implementation based on the
user-owned SpecQR algorithm and API contracts. It does not wrap, invoke,
or depend on another edition or a third-party QR encoder. No unsafe Rust,
FFI, external Cargo dependencies, generated native encoder, or runtime
resource downloads are required.

Behavioral baseline: SpecQR/SpecQR JavaScript revision
15ad15e5c770ea0e39072f8f88b2733018f02ffd (v3.0.0-rc.2).
Prior owner editions were inspected to preserve fixed API and safety rules:
Python 1deb5cf83ed7a93eeb44138e5980a963a00cdffb,
Java 1f2bf277a582f0eb4e31c9975443c1a76552aa23,
Kotlin 33a4d1963160fde5cf46fbd8b53331dcbe88f375.

QR structural, format/version BCH, Reed-Solomon, capacity and block tables
implement published QR Code Model 2 parameters. The fixed 6,953-scalar
Kanji mapping follows the owner's canonical WHATWG Encoding Standard
Shift_JIS first-mapping table, not a host locale codec. Decoded source-table
SHA-256: 90ede133127eca741de407d0f89cedbb4e3274a6308300207aea058df2151a87.

The URL adapter is an independent bounded standard-library implementation.
It does not implement the complete WHATWG/UTS #46 Unicode processing table.
See docs/gs1.md for exact supported behavior and audited differences.

Independent Nayuki, jsQR, ZXing-C++ and ZXing-Java encoders/decoders are
verification-only oracles. They are installed separately by development
scripts, never linked to or shipped as runtime Cargo dependencies. Their
licenses remain in their own distributions. No third-party QR source was
copied into the runtime.

Conservative Unicode hostname data is generated from Unicode 15.0.0
properties exposed by Python standard-library unicodedata. Unicode data
and software license is included in LICENSE-UNICODE. The generator is
tools/generate_idna_profile.py (SHA-256
0e182eef73a8016665539bac55840875a40b738b8485f41039726dcce5900bfe).
Generated semantic-record SHA-256:
04b9ad19e0ba108ed6c7e5368dd3bb2805313d9f25d9cd15465b919d7b59a5c7.
Runtime uses fixed lowercase/rejection/bidi data; it does not call Python.

